{"availability":"available","full":"evangelosvlachos96-dotcom/elevator-service-manager","name":"elevator-service-manager","description":"Django web app for an elevator maintenance company, manages clients, elevators, service visits, fault reports and Stripe payments.","category":"Business","language":"Python","stars":5,"forks":2,"created":"2026-05-15T02:51:21Z","updated":"2026-09-13T22:01:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://evangelosvlachos96-dotcom.github.io/elevator-service-manager/","topics":["client-portal","crm","dashboard","data-modeling","django","django-filter","django-framework","django-rest-framework","fault-reporting","function-based-views","internal-messaging","online-payments","open-source","python","role-based-access-control","shift-scheduling","sqlite","stripe-integration","webapp"],"demo":"https://evangelosvlachos96-dotcom.github.io/elevator-service-manager/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:18.405Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:18.405Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:18.405Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:24:18.405Z","stars":5,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Django web application for an elevator maintenance company. It lets the company manage its clients, their elevators and the service visits performed on them, while giving clients a portal to view their equipment, follow service history, report faults and pay for service online via Stripe.","The app has two kinds of users — company staff (technicians/office) and clients (elevator owners) — each with their own dashboard, and a built-in messaging system so the two sides can communicate (including photo-attached fault reports routed to whichever technician is on shift that day).","Originally built in 2021 (Django 3.1) and re-published with full documentation and the hardcoded secrets moved out of source control."],"features":["Role-based access — two user groups, Company (technicians/staff) and","Client, each with its own dashboard and permissions.","Client management — company staff can add, update and delete client accounts.","Elevator registry — each elevator (hydraulic or mechanical) is registered","against a client, with technical details such as motor cauldron, control panel, book code, wattage, stations, wire ropes and last KTEO inspection date."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/evangelosvlachos96-dotcom/elevator-service-manager/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4c89504e4f08828ee074ab6455aff0cf34d961d943abd86af0cdecfb0adee139","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:18.503Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:18.503Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A Django web application for an elevator maintenance company. It lets the company manage its clients, their elevators and the service visits performed on them, while giving clients a portal to view their equipment, follow service history, report faults and pay for service online via Stripe.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/evangelosvlachos96-dotcom/elevator-service-manager/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Assign your superuser to the Company group so you can log in to the staff dashboard.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/evangelosvlachos96-dotcom/elevator-service-manager/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The login page is the site root.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/evangelosvlachos96-dotcom/elevator-service-manager/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"4c89504e4f08828ee074ab6455aff0cf34d961d943abd86af0cdecfb0adee139","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/evangelosvlachos96-dotcom/elevator-service-manager/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:18.504Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-13T22:01:56Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/evangelosvlachos96-dotcom/elevator-service-manager/blob/main/README.md","checkedA